# Filling secrets in .env

When a secret, password, or API key is missing and Admin must supply it:

- Add the variable to `.env` yourself. Leave the value empty. Do not ask Admin to add the line.
- Quote the name when the value may contain spaces or `#`.
- Reply with the file path and the line number only. Do not print any secret already in the file.
- Admin types the value after `=` and replies that it is saved. Then load it without showing it.
- Do not invent an `.env` name the running service does not read. If the value lives in the database, say so, and still use one pre-filled `.env` line as the hand-off.
